ros-jazzy-rqt-execution-flow (0.2.0-1bookworm) bookworm; urgency=high

  * Flag slow or stuck calls: a configurable "Slow after" limit turns long-running
    calls red in the call tree and the flow view (#6 <https://github.com/nivednivu1997/rqt_execution_flow/issues/6>)
  * Statistics tab: calls, running, succeeded, canceled, failed, slow, average,
    95th-percentile and slowest time per action and service (#7 <https://github.com/nivednivu1997/rqt_execution_flow/issues/7>)
  * Click a node in the flow view to show only its calls (#8 <https://github.com/nivednivu1997/rqt_execution_flow/issues/8>)
  * "Show" list to filter calls by result: running, succeeded, canceled, failed,
    slow or problems; replaces "Hide finished" (#9 <https://github.com/nivednivu1997/rqt_execution_flow/issues/9>)
  * Colour nodes by role: action server, action client, service server,
    service client (#3 <https://github.com/nivednivu1997/rqt_execution_flow/issues/3>)
  * Keep cause and effect in the animation: a packet only leaves a node after
    earlier packets heading there have arrived (#3 <https://github.com/nivednivu1997/rqt_execution_flow/issues/3>)
  * Replay controls on their own row; the recording bar shows only the file name (#1 <https://github.com/nivednivu1997/rqt_execution_flow/issues/1>)
  * Clear warning when message types can't be loaded; fill in call types
    discovered after startup (#1 <https://github.com/nivednivu1997/rqt_execution_flow/issues/1>)
  * Documentation: service introspection for Python and C++, guides for every
    feature, new screenshots
  * Contributors: Nived Krishnan

 -- "Nived Krishnan" <nivednivu1997@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:30:00 -0000

